+//   S changes. op: 0 = push8, 1 = push16, 2 = pop8, 3 = pop16. s = S before the access. latched = a
+//   previous access was already refused. A refusal (false) performs no read/write, leaves S unchanged,
+//   latches gg_verify_stack_refused, and asks the debugger run loop to stop after this instruction.
+// gg_verify_io_observer: called for every CPU read/write of the hardware page ($FF bank) BEFORE the
+//   access (observation only; it cannot refuse).
+// gg_verify_pre_instruction: called at the start of every RunInstruction, before the instruction changes
+//   anything (the probe may also apply a harness-side MPR setting here). Returning false refuses the
+//   instruction before it executes (method A of #473, Issue #498): RunInstruction returns 0 cycles and
+//   requests a debugger-loop stop. Debugger build only: the patched RunInstruction refuses to compile with
+//   GG_DISABLE_DISASSEMBLER (#error), because without the stop request a refusal would never end the frame.
